 ## Background
-DAVIGS (Decoupling Appearance Variations In GS) was proposed by Dahmani et al. in 2024 [S1]. It addresses the limitations of existing Gaussian Splatting appearance modeling methods, which are either tightly coupled with the rendering process (hindering real-time rendering) or only account for mild global variations (performing poorly in scenes with local light changes) [S1]. The method builds on the 3D Gaussian Splatting framework [S1].
